### src/components/views/IFCTilesViewer.tsx
Main React component. Tab type: 'ifc-tiles'.

Phases:
  idle        File drop area + cached project list
  hashing     SHA-256 of IFC buffer (crypto.subtle)
  checking    IndexedDB lookup
  processing  Worker running (progress bar %)
  building    GLTFExporter building GLB tiles (main thread, 5 tiles/yield)
  streaming   Normal render loop
  error       Error message + retry

Three.js scene setup:
  WebGLRenderer  antialias + shadow maps (PCFSoft)
  HemisphereLight + DirectionalLight with shadow
  PerspectiveCamera  FOV 50, near 0.1, far 2000
  OrbitControls  damping 0.1, distance 0.5–800
  GridHelper  200m × 40 cells
  Fog  100–500m

TileStreamingManager (class inside component):
  Frustum test per tile bbox every requestAnimationFrame
  Sort load queue by camera distance (nearest first)
  Max 3 concurrent GLTFLoader.parse() calls
  LRU eviction when totalBytes > 512 MB
  LOD switch distance: 40m × 4 = 160m unload threshold
  BVH: geometry.computeBoundsTree() on every loaded mesh
  Floor filter: setFloorFilter(floorIds[]) — instantly evicts hidden floors

buildTileGLB(elements[]) → ArrayBuffer:
  Creates THREE.Scene from WorkerElementGeom[]
  MeshLambertMaterial with element color + transparency for windows/spaces
  mesh.userData = { expressID, category, name } → preserved in GLB extras
  GLTFExporter({ binary: true, embedImages: false })

Selection:
  raycaster.firstHitOnly = true  (three-mesh-bvh optimisation)
  Raycast against all loaded tile meshes
  hits[0].object.userData.expressID → ElementMeta lookup → properties panel

UI:
  Toolbar: project name, floor filter buttons (one per storey), stats, change file
  Drop zone: drag-and-drop + file input + cached project list with delete
  Progress overlay: phase label + message + animated progress bar
  Properties panel: category, name, IFC type, expressID, tile, custom properties

