## Roadmap / Next Steps

Phase 2 — Draco compression
  Add gltf-transform (@gltf-transform/core + @gltf-transform/extensions)
  Compress GLB before caching: transform → draco encoder → smaller IndexedDB size
  Decoder: DRACOLoader from three/examples/jsm already available

Phase 3 — LOD levels
  Worker generates 2 geometry sets: full detail (LOD0) + simplified (LOD1, 30% triangles)
  TileStreamingManager: load LOD1 first (fast), swap to LOD0 when dist < 30m

Phase 4 — Instancing detection
  Worker: hash geometry fingerprint per element type → detect identical shapes
  Replace N individual meshes with 1 THREE.InstancedMesh per unique geometry
  Reduces GPU draw calls for windows/doors/columns significantly

Phase 5 — Occlusion culling
  Integrate three-mesh-bvh OcclusionHelper or custom GPU readback
  Skip tiles fully behind other opaque tiles

Phase 6 — Web Worker pool
  Use Comlink or manual round-robin to run 2–4 Workers in parallel
  Divide IFC element types across workers → 2–4× faster initial processing
